    <bpmn:process id="W_W1183" name="W1183. Store Lease CAM Reconciliation, Rent Escalation &amp; Landlord Relationship Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual CAM reconciliation from landlord; scheduled rent escalation per lease; lease renewal negotiation; or landlord dispute
Frequency: Annual CAM reconciliation per lease; rent escalation per lease schedule (typically annual 3–5% increase); lease renewals every 3–5 years
Volume: 200 store leases + 4 DC leases + HQ office lease = ~205 active leases; ~50–70 CAM reconciliations/year; ~150–180 rent escalations/year (most leases escalate annually, per W1863)
Owner: Real Estate Manager
Participants: Real Estate Manager, Finance Controller, Legal, Store Manager, COO, Landlord Representative
Source: workflow W1183 — Store Lease CAM Reconciliation, Rent Escalation &amp; Landlord Relationship Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1183_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1183_Lane1" name="Real Estate Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1183_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1183_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1183_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1183_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1183_Lane2" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1183_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1183_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1183_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1183_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1183_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1183_Start5" name="Annual CAM reconciliation from landlord; scheduled rent escalation per lease; lease…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1183_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1183_Task6" name="Lease database maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Lease database maintenance: Real Estate Manager maintains master lease database in ERP: (a) lease term, renewal options, termination clauses; (b) base rent schedule with escalation dates and amounts; (c) CAM charge methodology (fixed, pro-rata share, actual pass-through); (d) RPT allocation; (e) tenant improvement allowance balance; (f) key dates: escalation, renewal notice, lease expiry; (g) system generates alerts 90 days before each key date
Responsible (R): Real Estate Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1183_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1183_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1183_Task7" name="Annual CAM reconciliation review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Annual CAM reconciliation review: When landlord submits annual CAM reconciliation statement: (a) Finance Controller reviews: (i) verify CAM calculation methodology matches lease terms; (ii) audit landlord&#x27;s supporting invoices for shared expenses — flag expenses that are landlord&#x27;s responsibility (structural repairs, roof replacement) vs. tenant responsibility; (iii) verify pro-rata share calculation (BuildRight&#x27;s leasable area ÷ total building area); (iv) compare to prior year — flag line items with &gt; 15% increase; (v) identify duplicate charges or expenses not authorized per lease; (b) for overcharges: Real Estate Manager files dispute with landlord within lease-specified dispute period (typically 30 days); (c) for undercharges: advise landlord of discrepancy to avoid future retroactive billing; (d) document agreed CAM amount and process adjustment payment or credit
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / Real Estate Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–8 hours/lease</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1183_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1183_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1183_Task8" name="Rent escalation validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Rent escalation validation: System calculates expected rent per escalation clause; Finance validates against landlord&#x27;s invoice: (a) verify escalation percentage matches lease (e.g., 3% annual compound increase); (b) recalculate base rent for new period; (c) if landlord&#x27;s invoiced amount exceeds calculated amount: dispute and request correction; (d) update lease database with new rent amount; (e) update store P&amp;L budget per W489 with escalated rent
Responsible (R): System / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): Real Estate Manager
Duration: 30 min/lease</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1183_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1183_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1183_Task9" name="Lease renewal negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Lease renewal negotiation: 90–180 days before lease expiry (per system alert): (a) Real Estate Manager assesses: store performance (revenue, margin, foot traffic), local market rental rates, alternative locations nearby, landlord relationship history; (b) negotiate renewal terms: (i) base rent — benchmark against market rate (PHP/sqm/month for comparable retail space in area); (ii) CAM cap — negotiate maximum annual CAM increase (e.g., capped at 5%); (iii) renewal term — seek 3–5 year renewal for stability; (iv) tenant improvement allowance — negotiate refresh allowance for store upgrades; (v) exclusive use clause — ensure landlord cannot lease adjacent space to direct competitor; (c) Legal reviews renewal agreement per W62; (d) COO approves renewal or directs closure per W807
Responsible (R): Real Estate Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 weeks/renewal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1183_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1183_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1183_Task10" name="Landlord relationship management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Landlord relationship management: (a) quarterly: Real Estate Manager conducts landlord satisfaction check-in: address maintenance issues, parking concerns, signage disputes, shared facility problems; (b) escalate unresolved issues to COO for executive-level landlord engagement; (c) maintain positive relationships for lease negotiations, CAM disputes, and emergency situations (e.g., building damage from typhoon requiring landlord structural repair); (d) annual landlord meeting for top-20 leases by value
Responsible (R): Real Estate Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1183_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1183_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1183_Task11" name="Monthly rent &amp; CAM payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly rent &amp; CAM payment: (a) system generates monthly rent and CAM payment schedule per lease; (b) AP processes payment per W7 with automatic GL coding to store cost center; (c) for BuildRight Property Management, Inc. leases: intercompany settlement per W87; (d) track rent expense per store for P&amp;L reporting per W102
Responsible (R): System / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1183_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1183_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1183_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1183_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1183_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-218 (ensure facility compliance &amp; lease-cost integrity.) | - operational: Real Estate Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Real Estate Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1183_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1183_Annotation13" targetRef="W1183_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
