    <bpmn:process id="W_W1446" name="W1446. Store Lease Renewal Negotiation, Market Rent Benchmarking &amp; Strategic Exit or Relocation Decision" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Lease expiration within 12 months; or landlord-initiated renegotiation; or store performance review triggering location reassessment
Frequency: ~20–30 lease renewals/year (assuming 200 stores with average 7–10 year lease terms; some leases may be shorter or negotiated mid-term)
Volume: Each renewal involves 1 store location; ~20–30 renewal decisions/year; ~5–10 of these may involve strategic exit or relocation evaluation
Owner: COO &amp; Construction
Participants: COO, Real Estate Manager, Finance Controller, VP Store Operations, Store Manager (performance input), Legal Counsel, External Real Estate Broker (market data)
Source: workflow W1446 — Store Lease Renewal Negotiation, Market Rent Benchmarking &amp; Strategic Exit or Relocation Decision</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1446_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1446_Lane1" name="Real Estate Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1446_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1446_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1446_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1446_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1446_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1446_Lane2" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1446_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1446_Lane3" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1446_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1446_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1446_Start5" name="Lease expiration within 12 months; or landlord-initiated renegotiation; or store…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1446_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1446_Task6" name="Lease expiration inventory and prioritization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Lease expiration inventory and prioritization: Real Estate Manager maintains rolling lease expiration calendar: (a) identify all leases expiring in the next 12–18 months, (b) prioritize by: (i) annual rent value (higher rent = higher financial impact), (ii) store performance (underperforming stores need deeper assessment), (iii) landlord relationship (difficult landlords require earlier engagement), (c) assign each renewal to a negotiation track: (i) standard renewal (performing store, fair market rent), (ii) renegotiation (performing store but above-market rent), (iii) relocation evaluation (underperforming store), (iv) exit evaluation (market no longer viable)
Responsible (R): Real Estate Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1446_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1446_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1446_Task7" name="Store performance assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store performance assessment: VP Store Operations and Finance Controller assess each store&#x27;s performance: (a) sales performance: (i) actual vs. plan (Year-over-Year), (ii) sales per sqm vs. chain average, (iii) same-store sales growth trend (3-year), (b) profitability: (i) store-level EBITDA margin, (ii) rent-to-revenue ratio (target: &lt; 5% of revenue), (c) strategic value: (i) market coverage (does closing this store create a coverage gap?), (ii) competitive presence (does this store prevent competitor entry into the market?), (iii) brand visibility in the community
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 week per batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1446_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1446_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1446_Task8" name="Market rent benchmarking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Market rent benchmarking: Real Estate Manager benchmarks current lease terms against market: (a) comparable retail space rental rates in the same area (from broker data, property listings, industry reports), (b) commercial real estate market trends in the region (rising/falling/stable), (c) assess if current rent is: (i) below market (landlord likely to push for increase), (ii) at market (fair renewal), (iii) above market (BuildRight should negotiate reduction), (d) calculate rent impact on store P&amp;L under different scenarios (market rate, 10% increase, 10% decrease)
Responsible (R): Real Estate Manager / External Broker
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 week per batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1446_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1446_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1446_Task9" name="Renewal negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Renewal negotiation: For stores where renewal is recommended: (a) Real Estate Manager initiates negotiation with landlord: (i) present market rent data supporting BuildRight&#x27;s position, (ii) negotiate: base rent, escalation formula (fixed % vs. CPI-linked), CAM caps, tenant improvement allowance, exclusivity renewal, lease term (longer term in exchange for lower rent), (b) Legal Counsel reviews lease renewal terms: (i) confirm renewal option language matches original lease, (ii) identify any unfavorable terms to renegotiate, (iii) ensure assignment/sublease rights are preserved, (c) target outcomes: (i) rent at or below market, (ii) annual escalation capped at 3–5%, (iii) 5–10 year renewal term, (iv) tenant improvement allowance for store refresh
Responsible (R): Real Estate Manager / Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1446_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1446_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1446_Task10" name="Relocation evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Relocation evaluation (for underperforming stores): If store performance assessment (Step 2) indicates the location is the primary cause of underperformance: (a) Real Estate Manager identifies 2–3 alternative sites within the same market area, (b) compare: (i) new site lease cost vs. current site (including estimated moving cost and downtime), (ii) new site traffic and accessibility advantages, (iii) financial model: projected performance at new site vs. current site, (c) if relocation is more profitable than renewal: execute new site lease per W1445 and plan store closure per W703 with transition to new location, (d) if renewal is more profitable despite underperformance: negotiate rent reduction as condition for renewal
Responsible (R): Real Estate Manager / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1446_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1446_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1446_Task11" name="Decision and execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Decision and execution: (a) COO presents recommendation to CEO: (i) renew at negotiated terms, (ii) relocate to alternative site, or (iii) exit market, (b) CEO approves; Legal Counsel executes renewal or new lease, (c) if relocating or exiting: VP Store Operations activates W703 (store closure/transition) timeline, (d) update lease tracker and financial projections for the location
Responsible (R): COO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1446_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1446_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1446_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1446_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1446_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-301 (ensure controlled execution — Site Selection &amp; Lease Management (PA-20.1).) | - operational: COO &amp; Construction review and approval gate
Owner: COO &amp; Construction</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
